        id: "attack-drones",
        status: "open", size: "large", order: 8,
        title: "Brains fly attack drones: multirotor strike drones (and swarms of them), and an armed fixed-wing UAV, against the guns and fighters we already built",
        why: "Keith, for later consideration: \"Brains fly attack drones.\" AMBIGUOUS, SAID PLAINLY: it could mean small multirotor strike drones (FPV / loitering munitions, flown in numbers), an armed medium-altitude UAV of the Reaper kind, or both; the slices below cover both and the first can ship without the second. The tree has no vehicle model for either (the word appears only in themes and HUD text).",
        note: "PROGRESS (unnumbered, on the working branch, nothing shipped; Keith asked for the flight and the trainings: 'let's also do the drone trainings too'): THE FLIGHT AND TRAINING SLICES ARE BUILT. THE WEAPONS AND ENGAGEMENT SLICES ARE NOT, AND ARE NOT TO BE BUILT -- a strike drone or kamikaze, a counter-drone fight, an armed UAV, swarms as weapons: the territory a safety classifier stopped for the helicopter's weapons, and not what was asked for. BUILT: (1) physics/mechanics/multirotorModel6dof.mjs (four motors with lag, a mixer, reaction torque and rotor inertia, a battery that sags and cuts off, legs with friction, a named fate for the first contact; 76 rows, 108 sabotages); (2) brain/autopilotDrone.mjs (a cascade of tilt, velocity, altitude and heading; landing; a motor-out policy that gives up the yaw; 42 rows, 70 sabotages, 20 of which went 0 red the first time and each got a row); (3) brain/droneTask.mjs (hover, recovery, go-to and motor-out scenarios; a landing is charged its sink and its ground speed, a crash its speed; 72 rows, 140 sabotages, three equivalent and said so; it found that a flight from a non-finite state scored NaN, now charged the worst crash); (4) brain/pilotDronePolicy.mjs (the Giant Fiber Circuit as the quadrotor pilot, 54 rows, 84 sabotages) and brain/pilotDroneMlp.mjs (the 20 -> 32 -> 32 -> 4 perceptron, 31 rows, 40 sabotages), both with hand weights that are the hand pilot to float32; (5) tools/ship/trainDronePilot.mjs and its command trainPilotDrone.mjs (the helicopter's recipe and qualification rule; 67 rows, 40 sabotages and 17 on the shipped file). RESULTS: THE HAND PILOT LOSES EVERY MOTOR-OUT FLIGHT -- all 162 on the eight sets crash, at 14 to 42 m/s (the quadrotor's dead man's curve, pinned in the gate) -- and flies the other kinds to the end. THE FRUIT FLY DOES NOT QUALIFY AND NOTHING IS WRITTEN: its champion (seed 8000, 196 of 1,167 weights moved) takes the motor-out audit from -6.70 to -5.70 (18 not standing of 20 against 20) and loses the rest -- hover -0.525 against -0.477, recovery -0.651 against -0.608, go-to -2.047 against -1.953, each past the 0.02 floor -- and ends one safety-audit flight the hand pilot completes. The cause looks like the objective and not the rule: 12 of the 34 training scenarios are motor-out flights, so the search trades the other kinds for them; a per-kind balanced objective with fresh audit seeds is the follow-up (the fruit fly's audit is spent). THE GPU NETWORK QUALIFIES AND IS WRITTEN (brain/pilotDroneMlpWeightsDefault.json, seed 9002, 87 of 1,860 weights differ from the hand pilot's): audit -3.261 against -3.616 (18 scenarios better, 11 worse), reserve -2.614 against -3.118, hover, recovery and go-to within the floor, no safety-audit flight ended that the hand pilot completes. *** BUT THE MOTOR-OUT CORNER IS NOT SOLVED: all twenty motor-out audit flights still end crashed, for it as for the hand pilot; the whole gain is a SLOWER CRASH (a mean of 23.1 m/s at contact against 32.0; six of its crashes are 'hard landing', a leg took it, where all twenty of the hand pilot's are the hull). *** The file's own text says so, and the gate re-measures every number in it. THE SECOND RECIPE, RUN WITHOUT LOOSENING A RULE (tools/ship/trainDronePilot.mjs --guard 0.01 --sets v2: DT.guarded refuses a child whose hover, recovery or go-to mean on the TRAINING scenarios falls more than 0.01 below the hand pilot's, and five fresh sets are read once): BOTH NETWORKS NOW QUALIFY AND ARE WRITTEN BESIDE THE FIRST FILES, NOT OVER THEM -- brain/pilotDroneWeightsV2.json (141 of 1,167 weights differ; seed 8102) and brain/pilotDroneMlpWeightsV2.json (167 of 1,860; seed 9101). The first retrain's failure was the objective and not the rule, as suspected. THE FRUIT FLY: audit -3.422 against the hand pilot's -3.796 (13 scenarios better, 7 worse), reserve -3.037 against -3.266, hover, recovery and go-to inside the 0.02 floor; its motor-out gain is again a SLOWER CRASH (a mean of 26.5 m/s at contact against 37.0; none of the twenty stands). THE GPU NETWORK: audit -2.883 against -3.738 (12 better, 8 worse), reserve -3.233 against -3.266, 28 safety-audit flights ended early against 30; ITS MOTOR-OUT GAIN IS PARTLY REAL -- three of the twenty audit motor-out flights END STANDING (landed at 3.8 to 5.9 m/s; the hand pilot lands none, and the first GPU file none), seventeen do not, and the mean contact speed is 22.0 m/s against 35.3. That is one audit of twenty flights: the three is a measurement and not a rate, and THE CORNER IS STILL NOT SOLVED. The v2 and v1 files are NOT compared head to head (other audits, other hand baselines: the GPU network's audit gain is +0.855 here against +0.355 for the first file, and that is not a like-for-like figure). A DEFECT THE NEW TRAINER ROWS FOUND: `--workers` did not hand `--guard` to its child processes, so a four-process guarded run would have trained the first recipe under the second recipe's name; fixed, with a row. No page, roster or arena uses the drone files yet (flight and training only). When this round ships, flip the weapons slices to `wont` here with that reason. THE ORIGINAL READING FOLLOWS. NOT SCOPED WITH KEITH; THIS IS MY READING, TO BE CORRECTED. LIKELY SLICES. (1) THE MULTIROTOR: physics/mechanics/multirotorModel6dof.mjs on rigidBody6dof -- four (or six) rotor thrusts and their reaction torques through a motor mixer, a battery that runs down (energy is the resource that ammo is not, as the gunner trainer found), tiny mass and inertia so it turns in a fraction of a second. Its controls are the four motor commands, which the brain's outputs can BE (a 4-output network with hand weights that are the mixer) -- the first customer of a policy that flies the motors, not the attitude. (2) THE HAND PILOT AND THE BRAINS: a cascaded hand controller written through the network, the fruit fly and the GPU network trained from it with the existing recipe, held-out and audit seeds, a file only if it beats the hand pilot. (3) SWARMS: N drones against a target and against guns -- the multi-craft arena (spaceArena, dogfightArena) already holds any number of crafts and teams; what is new is a swarm tactic (the hand rule: spread, converge, break off when hit) and a count in the page. A STRIKE DRONE IS A WEAPON AND A VEHICLE AT ONCE: ramming damage already exists (spaceArena RAM_DAMAGE), so a kamikaze is a pilot whose goal is the collision, scored by what it destroyed. (4) THE COUNTER: the battleship's point-defence seats and the fighters' guns against a drone swarm are the cheapest honest first fight -- the gunner networks can be trained on it, and the finding to look for is how many small fast targets thirteen seats can stop. (5) THE ARMED UAV: flightModel6dof with a different spec (long wings, low speed, high endurance) and a gun or missile pod; the brains and the page are the ones already built. Depends on attack-helicopters only for the shared weapons slice (rockets, a seeker).",
        evidence: "node -e 'const fs=require(\"fs\");const hit=fs.readdirSync(\"physics/mechanics\").filter((f)=>/quad|multirotor|drone|uav/i.test(f));console.log(\"drone models in physics/mechanics:\",hit.length)'   # 2 today (the model and its gate); was 0 when the item was written",
