        id: "terrain-in-flight-models",
        status: "open", size: "large", order: 12,
        title: "Solid terrain in the flight models and on the pages: the ground is a height function, not z = 0",
        why: "Found while gating the helicopter pilot: every flight model's ground is the flat plane z = 0 (flightModel6dof says so in its header; rotorcraftModel6dof's skids and fate read z = 0), so a ridge or a wall is a function only the PILOT is handed (brain/autopilotRotor.mjs reads `terrain(x, y)` and keeps its skids off it) and the machine flies THROUGH it when the pilot fails -- the gate had to measure 'clearance goes negative' instead of 'crashes'. The helicopter arena (item attack-helicopters, slice 5) needs terrain, the sky/weather item wants ground to cast haze on, and the aeroplane pilots 'do not look at the ground'.",
        note: "PROGRESS (unnumbered, on the working branch, nothing shipped): DONE -- physics/mechanics/terrain.mjs (a JSON-spec height function with height, gradient and normal; FLAT is the bit-for-bit fast path, so every existing flight is unchanged; fbm, ridge and wall kinds; meshOf builds a page's vertex grid; its own gate with sabotages), the contact tests in BOTH models (flightModel6dof and rotorcraftModel6dof read the surface under each contact point, the skid friction is along the slope, and the helicopter's fate names a slope steeper than 15 degrees; the aeroplane's touchdown limit stays 5 degrees), and the helicopter pilot (brain/autopilotRotor.mjs flies over a surface with a 360 m look-ahead that bisects to find where an obstacle STARTS, after real-collision flights showed the sampled look-ahead saw a wall up to 100 m late; a wall 60 m off is flown into without the law and the pilot stops 17 m short with it). REMAINING: (a) THE AEROPLANE PILOTS GAIN A GROUND-AVOIDANCE LAW the way autopilotRotor.mjs has one (a look-ahead floor), which changes their baselines -- so it is its own round with its own re-audit of the shipped pilots, said before it is started; (b) THE PAGE MESH: a Three mesh from meshOf on the helicopter page (attack-helicopters slice 6) and as an option on es-flight6dof -- DEFERRED ON PURPOSE, because the flight page's pixel rows and its ~85 s gate would move, and nothing needs the mesh until the arena exists. ORIGINAL SCOPE: one `terrain(x, y) -> height` (and a slope, for a skid's contact normal) shared by the models, the pilots and the renderer; the default is the flat zero so nothing existing moves.",
